cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the archived release corresponding to
  the version you used. Zenodo release archives will be linked from the repository.
type: software
title: "Notandia browser extension: publisher context and research-integrity signals"
authors:
  - family-names: Marcolongo
    given-names: Mario
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2846-7115"
abstract: >-
  Notandia is an independent, open-source browser extension for configurable
  publisher context, citation navigation and optional post-publication checks
  using Crossref and NCBI metadata. It continues the MDPI Filter project.
  Watchlist matches are contextual signals, not article-quality scores, and an
  absence of notices does not establish reliability. This repository contains
  the browser extension; the Notandia Zotero plugin is maintained separately.
  Code is licensed under AGPL-3.0-or-later. The logo and bundled community data
  retain their separate CC BY-SA 4.0 licences and attribution notices.
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/notandia/browser-extension"
url: "https://notandia.pages.dev/"
keywords:
  - research integrity
  - scholarly communication
  - browser extension
  - citation navigation
  - post-publication notices
  - publisher context
# Release-specific version and date are deliberately omitted here so a later
# GitHub release cannot inherit a stale version/date from this citation file.
